{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS7KQq6y4Srn6Bane5KS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All six events from `docs/EVENTS.md` are now wired up through `Analytics.capture`. Event names and properties match the spec exactly, and no email or phone value is sent. `flutter analyze` reports no issues, but I haven't run the app or written tests, so the number of events actually sent hasn't been checked.\n\n| Event | When it fires |\n|---|---|\n| `registration_email_started` | The first time the email field is edited, not on every keystroke |\n| `registration_phone_started` | The first time the phone field is edited, not on every keystroke |\n| `loan_amount_changed` (`amount`) | When the user lets go of the slider, so once per drag or tap |\n| `terms_accepted` | Only when the box is ticked, not when it's unticked |\n| `registration_continue_tapped` (`amount`, `terms`) | On each tap of Continue, before going to the offers screen |\n| `offers_scrolled` (`offset`) | When a scroll comes to a stop, so once per scroll gesture rather than every frame |\n\n**The colleague's note:** it applies here, since this is Flutter, it uses PostHog and the README says you're on the free tier. Taken literally, the spec (\"started typing\", \"moved the slider\", \"scrolled\") would send an event per keystroke or per frame. I used the note's once-only flags for the text fields, the release-the-slider hook, the scroll-stop hook, and kept the names unchanged. Its focus-based events and \"send the final value\" step didn't apply, because the spec has no such events. I skipped its PostHog debug and dashboard checks.\n\n**Questions for product** (also listed in `ANSWER.md`):\n- **\"Started typing\" doesn't fire again after Back:** the registration screen stays alive while the offers screen is open, so going back and typing again sends nothing new. That seems right for a funnel, but ask product if they meant once per visit.\n- **`terms_accepted` can repeat:** it fires each time the box is ticked again after unticking.\n- **`offers_scrolled` volume:** it fires once per scroll, not once per visit. If product only needs to know whether people scrolled, sending it once per visit would cut the count further.\n\n`analysis_options.yaml` changed while I was working (a list of excluded folders was added). That wasn't me, so I left it alone. I deleted the `pubspec.lock` and `.dart_tool/` files that running the analyzer created. Nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1478,"cache_read_input_tokens":29777,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1478},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2cbb8c1e-eddc-4efa-9c8f-bd6eb90ba272","uuid":"50b66498-c3ce-4a8e-8301-42d0e06d23a5","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:27:43.868Z","request_id":"req_011CgS7KQKLogMN46317rofE"}
